{"status":"ok","message-type":"work-list","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"facets":{},"total-results":106239,"items":[{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,3,18]],"date-time":"2026-03-18T13:08:23Z","timestamp":1773839303116,"version":"3.50.1"},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"Canadian Center of Science and Education","issue":"2","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2018,3,15]],"date-time":"2018-03-15T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1521072000000},"content-version":"unspecified","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"http:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/4.0"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["APR"],"abstract":"<jats:p>We prove that all the Faulhaber coefficients of a sum of odd power of elements of an arithmetic progression may simply be calculated from only one of them which is easily calculable from two Bernoulli polynomials as so as from power sums of integers. This gives two simple formulae for calculating them. As for sums related to even powers, they may be calculated simply from those related to the nearest odd one\u2019s.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.5539\/apr.v10n2p5","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2018,3,21]],"date-time":"2018-03-21T13:31:04Z","timestamp":1521639064000},"page":"5","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":1,"title":["The Faulhaber Problem on Sums of Powers on Arithmetic Progressions Resolved"],"prefix":"10.5539","volume":"10","author":[{"given":"Do","family":"Tan Si","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"3486","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2018,3,15]]},"container-title":["Applied Physics Research"],"link":[{"URL":"http:\/\/www.ccsenet.org\/journal\/index.php\/apr\/article\/viewFile\/73113\/40889","content-type":"application\/pdf","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"text-mining"},{"URL":"https:\/\/www.ccsenet.org\/journal\/index.php\/APR\/article\/download\/73113\/40889","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2025,12,4]],"date-time":"2025-12-04T23:44:30Z","timestamp":1764891870000},"score":32.900883,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"http:\/\/www.ccsenet.org\/journal\/index.php\/apr\/article\/view\/73113"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2018,3,15]]},"references-count":0,"journal-issue":{"issue":"2","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2018,2,27]]}},"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.5539\/apr.v10n2p5","ISSN":["1916-9647","1916-9639"],"issn-type":[{"value":"1916-9647","type":"electronic"},{"value":"1916-9639","type":"print"}],"published":{"date-parts":[[2018,3,15]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,8]],"date-time":"2026-10-08T07:47:12Z","timestamp":1791445632182,"version":"4.3.3"},"reference-count":8,"publisher":"American Mathematical Society (AMS)","issue":"203","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["Math. Comp."],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[1993]]},"abstract":"<p>\n                    Early 17th-century mathematical publications of Johann Faulhaber contain some remarkable theorems, such as the fact that the\n                    <italic>r<\/italic>\n                    -fold summation of\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math\/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1998\/Math\/MathML\" alttext=\"1 Superscript m Baseline comma 2 Superscript m Baseline comma ellipsis comma n Superscript m\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                              <mml:msup>\n                                <mml:mn>1<\/mml:mn>\n                                <mml:mi>m<\/mml:mi>\n                              <\/mml:msup>\n                            <\/mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mo>,<\/mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                              <mml:msup>\n                                <mml:mn>2<\/mml:mn>\n                                <mml:mi>m<\/mml:mi>\n                              <\/mml:msup>\n                            <\/mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mo>,<\/mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mo>\n                              \u2026\n                              \n                            <\/mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mo>,<\/mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                              <mml:msup>\n                                <mml:mi>n<\/mml:mi>\n                                <mml:mi>m<\/mml:mi>\n                              <\/mml:msup>\n                            <\/mml:mrow>\n                          <\/mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application\/x-tex\">{1^m},{2^m}, \\ldots ,{n^m}<\/mml:annotation>\n                        <\/mml:semantics>\n                      <\/mml:math>\n                    <\/inline-formula>\n                    is a polynomial in\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math\/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1998\/Math\/MathML\" alttext=\"n left-parenthesis n plus r right-parenthesis\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mi>n<\/mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">(<\/mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>n<\/mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo>+<\/mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>r<\/mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">)<\/mml:mo>\n                          <\/mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application\/x-tex\">n(n + r)<\/mml:annotation>\n                        <\/mml:semantics>\n                      <\/mml:math>\n                    <\/inline-formula>\n                    when\n                    <italic>m<\/italic>\n                    is a positive odd number. The present paper explores a computation-based approach by which Faulhaber may well have discovered such results, and solves a 360-year-old riddle that Faulhaber presented to his readers. It also shows that similar results hold when we express the sums in terms of central factorial powers instead of ordinary powers. Faulhaber\u2019s coefficients can moreover be generalized to noninteger exponents, obtaining asymptotic series for\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math\/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1998\/Math\/MathML\" alttext=\"1 Superscript alpha Baseline plus 2 Superscript alpha Baseline plus midline-horizontal-ellipsis plus n Superscript alpha\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                              <mml:msup>\n                                <mml:mn>1<\/mml:mn>\n                                <mml:mi>\n                                  \u03b1\n                                  \n                                <\/mml:mi>\n                              <\/mml:msup>\n                            <\/mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mo>+<\/mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                              <mml:msup>\n                                <mml:mn>2<\/mml:mn>\n                                <mml:mi>\n                                  \u03b1\n                                  \n                                <\/mml:mi>\n                              <\/mml:msup>\n                            <\/mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mo>+<\/mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mo>\n                              \u22ef\n                              \n                            <\/mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mo>+<\/mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                              <mml:msup>\n                                <mml:mi>n<\/mml:mi>\n                                <mml:mi>\n                                  \u03b1\n                                  \n                                <\/mml:mi>\n                              <\/mml:msup>\n                            <\/mml:mrow>\n                          <\/mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application\/x-tex\">{1^\\alpha } + {2^\\alpha } + \\cdots + {n^\\alpha }<\/mml:annotation>\n                        <\/mml:semantics>\n                      <\/mml:math>\n                    <\/inline-formula>\n                    in powers of\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math\/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1998\/Math\/MathML\" alttext=\"n Superscript negative 1 Baseline left-parenthesis n plus 1 right-parenthesis Superscript negative 1\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                              <mml:msup>\n                                <mml:mi>n<\/mml:mi>\n                                <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                                  <mml:mo>\n                                    \u2212\n                                    \n                                  <\/mml:mo>\n                                  <mml:mn>1<\/mml:mn>\n                                <\/mml:mrow>\n                              <\/mml:msup>\n                            <\/mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                              <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">(<\/mml:mo>\n                              <mml:mi>n<\/mml:mi>\n                              <mml:mo>+<\/mml:mo>\n                              <mml:mn>1<\/mml:mn>\n                              <mml:msup>\n                                <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">)<\/mml:mo>\n                                <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                                  <mml:mo>\n                                    \u2212\n                                    \n                                  <\/mml:mo>\n                                  <mml:mn>1<\/mml:mn>\n                                <\/mml:mrow>\n                              <\/mml:msup>\n                            <\/mml:mrow>\n                          <\/mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application\/x-tex\">{n^{ - 1}}{(n + 1)^{ - 1}}<\/mml:annotation>\n                        <\/mml:semantics>\n                      <\/mml:math>\n                    <\/inline-formula>\n                    .\n                  <\/p>","DOI":"10.1090\/s0025-5718-1993-1197512-7","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2010,6,28]],"date-time":"2010-06-28T16:05:58Z","timestamp":1277741158000},"page":"277-294","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":115,"title":["Johann Faulhaber and sums of powers"],"prefix":"10.1090","volume":"61","author":[{"given":"Donald E.","family":"Knuth","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"14","reference":[{"issue":"6","key":"1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"451","DOI":"10.2307\/2323466","article-title":"A quick route to sums of powers","volume":"93","author":"Edwards, A. W. F.","year":"1986","journal-title":"Amer. Math. Monthly","ISSN":"https:\/\/id.crossref.org\/issn\/0002-9890","issn-type":"print"},{"key":"2","unstructured":"Johann Faulhaber, Academia Algebr\u0153, Darinnen die miraculosische Inventiones zu den h\u00f6chsten Cossen weiters continuirt und profitiert werden, call number QA154.8 F3 1631a f MATH at Stanford University Libraries, Johann Ulrich Sch\u00f6nigs, Augspurg [sic], 1631."},{"issue":"10","key":"3","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-